# .gitattributes — repository line-ending policy.
# Brief: win-line-endings-gitattributes-pin (Windows fleet).
#
# WHY: SKYCOT is developed on macOS/Linux (LF) but builds + runs on Windows.
# Several file classes are BYTE-SENSITIVE — their exact bytes are embedded into
# the binary (`include_str!` / `include_bytes!`), hashed into the audit chain,
# or compared byte-for-byte as golden fixtures. A CRLF silently introduced on a
# Windows checkout or commit (git's `core.autocrlf=true` is the common Windows
# default) would change those bytes and cause Windows-ONLY corruption / test
# flakiness. CRLF was hypothesised as a failure cause 3x during the Windows
# hardening session (it never actually was — each was a real bug or stale
# literal); these rules foreclose the class for good by pinning such files to
# LF in BOTH the repo and the working tree, so a Windows checkout is
# byte-identical to a macOS/Linux one.
#
# SCOPE (deliberately surgical): we enumerate the byte-sensitive + source/data/
# text classes and force them to LF (`text eol=lf`), and mark true binaries
# `binary` so git never touches their bytes. We do NOT set a repo-wide
# `* text=auto eol=lf` default — that would entangle the one pre-existing CRLF
# asset (`web/public/logos/calendly.svg`) and force a renormalisation diff.
# Every tracked file matched below is already LF today (`git ls-files --eol`),
# so this commit introduces ZERO content change — it is purely a forward guard.
# See docs/skycot/windows/LINE-ENDINGS.md for the policy + the calendly.svg note.

# --- Byte-sensitive: embedded in the binary / hashed / golden fixtures ---
*.sql      text eol=lf
*.jsonl    text eol=lf
*.json     text eol=lf
*.toml     text eol=lf
*.csv      text eol=lf
*.snap     text eol=lf

# --- Source (inline SQL strings + golden string literals live here) ---
*.rs       text eol=lf
*.sh       text eol=lf
*.ps1      text eol=lf
*.py       text eol=lf
*.js       text eol=lf
*.mjs      text eol=lf
*.cjs      text eol=lf
*.ts       text eol=lf
*.tsx      text eol=lf
*.jsx      text eol=lf
*.css      text eol=lf
*.scss     text eol=lf
*.html     text eol=lf

# --- Docs / config text ---
*.md       text eol=lf
*.yml      text eol=lf
*.yaml     text eol=lf
*.txt      text eol=lf
*.lock     text eol=lf

# --- True binaries: never apply EOL conversion ---
*.png      binary
*.jpg      binary
*.jpeg     binary
*.gif      binary
*.ico      binary
*.webp     binary
*.pdf      binary
*.mp4      binary
*.mov      binary
*.woff     binary
*.woff2    binary
*.ttf      binary
*.otf      binary
*.eot      binary
*.zip      binary
*.gz       binary
*.tar      binary
*.db       binary
*.wasm     binary
*.bin      binary
